53048274 (3110 1792849325553 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f331") (src . "test: retire-race waits on a monotonic clock, not a spin count\n\nThe fixture's three waits on a child's trace (the retirer's `retire-locked`,\nthe writer's `lock-wait`, and W6b's `barrier before-retire`) were shell\nspins of 300000 and 400000 iterations. A spin measures the machine, not the\ntime: on a slow runner the writer had not reached its `flock` when the spin\nran out, the report read `no` while the retirer sat inside the lock, and\nthe fixture alone was green.\n\n- One procedure, `trace-poll`, writes all three polls: one perl process on\n  CLOCK_MONOTONIC that looks at the trace file every 50 ms, answers `yes`\n  at the first look that finds the word, and `no` only from a look taken\n  after the bound (20 s); a poll that cannot run prints nothing, so its\n  report line matches no row. What discriminates is unchanged: with the\n  lock removed `lock-wait` never appears and the row still reads `no`.\n- A CONTROL pins the bound: the writer replaced by `true`, bound 2 s; the\n  poll must end by itself, read `no`, take at least the bound and end well\n  before a fixed 20 s.\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: retire-race 19 23.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 468))))
